prompt_template:
Each item below is a first-person health question written in careful everyday English. Rewrite each one the way the same person would quickly type it into a chat app on their phone.

Keep exactly:
- every fact: who, symptoms, how long, how often, how bad, what helps or worsens, what they are asking;
- the order of the facts;
- every word they use. You may change capital letters, drop apostrophes (im, dont, its), and add a few small joining words (and, so, but) where you join sentences. Never replace a word with another and never use a medical term the original does not use.

Make it read like real phone typing:
- all lower case;
- very little punctuation: at most one comma and at most one full stop inside the message. Run sentences together instead. Keep a question mark at the end if the original asks a question;
- start the message with the person's own first words. Do not start with ok so, so, idk, hey, hi, um, well or any other opener;
- messages should differ from each other in rhythm; do not give them all the same shape.

Do not:
- add or drop any fact, symptom or number;
- add slang, emoji or misspellings;
- make it shorter by leaving words out.

Return ONLY a JSON array with one object per item, in the same order, each with exactly the fields "id" (copied unchanged) and "text" (the rewrite). No prose.

